================================================================================
THIRD-PARTY SKILLS — the MIT grant above does NOT cover these
================================================================================

`skills/` bundles material from several origins. The MIT license above applies
to the packaging (installer, doctor, tests, connectors, docs) and to skills
authored for this toolkit. Individual skills carry their own `license:` field
in their `SKILL.md`, and that field governs.

Known non-MIT skills, as declared in their own front matter:

  Proprietary — "LICENSE.txt has complete terms" (bundled Claude skills):
    skills/docx      skills/pdf      skills/pptx      skills/xlsx

  Proprietary (toolkit-internal; not for redistribution outside the lab
  without the author's permission):
    skills/experiment-hub      skills/primer-design

  Apache-2.0 / BSD-3-Clause / MIT (per-skill, see each SKILL.md):
    the remaining skills, several of which are authored by K-Dense Inc.

Before redistributing this package — especially publicly — re-read each
`SKILL.md` front matter rather than assuming the repository-level MIT applies.
A repository-wide license claim that contradicts a bundled skill's own terms is
a licensing defect, not a formality.
